//! The `modifiers` / `economy` ORACLE document (`roblox/test/modifiers_test.luau`).
//!
//! `roblox/test/modifiers_test.luau` asserts the Luau port of `Modifiers.luau` +
//! `Economy.luau` against a document of expected values. Every one of those values
//! is produced HERE, by running the real Rust — never hand-derived
//! (`roblox/CONTRACTS.md` C4, `roblox/SIM-SPEC.md` §S1).
//!
//! ## Why this lives inside the lib
//!
//! The document used to be generated by a throwaway crate outside the repo taking a
//! path dependency on `sim`. That worked for the parts reachable through `pub` API —
//! `Modifiers::{apply_effect, damage_mult, …}` — and *could not* work for the rest:
//! `modifiers::apply_ramps` and every `economy::*` entry point are `pub(crate)`, so
//! an external crate cannot call them at all. Those two arrays were therefore
//! "carried forward verbatim" from an older pass and went stale the moment the
//! balance changed underneath them.
//!
//! Putting the generator in the lib fixes that without widening a single item's
//! visibility: a module inside `sim` may call `pub(crate)` items directly. The whole
//! document is regenerable from one command and "carried forward verbatim" no longer
//! exists.
//!
//! ## Invariants
//!
//! - **Every expected value comes out of running the Rust.** Nothing below writes an
//!   expectation by hand; the tables here are the case *inputs* only.
//! - **Deterministic**: no wall-clock, no `HashMap` iteration, no platform RNG. The
//!   only RNG is the arena's own seeded `rng_proc`, driven from a fixed seed per case.
//! - No floats: every `Fixed` is emitted as its 16-digit two's-complement raw, so a
//!   divergence in the port is a bit-level divergence rather than an "about right".
//! - Case NAMES and case ORDER are part of the contract — the Luau tags every
//!   assertion with them. Add cases; do not reorder or rename them.

